{% doc %}
  @description Resolve the active captcha provider key. Values are normalized — trimmed and
    lowercased — so an explicit ' SomeProvider ' or a CAPTCHA_DEFAULT_PROVIDER constant saved
    with stray whitespace/capitals still resolves. The abstraction ships no provider of its own:
    when neither an explicit value nor the constant is present this returns blank, and the
    availability gate (helpers/provider_available) fails gracefully downstream.
  @param {string} [provider] Explicit provider key; used when present.
  @returns {string} provider key — explicit value, else the CAPTCHA_DEFAULT_PROVIDER constant, else '' (normalized).
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign resolved = provider | strip | downcase
  assign resolved = resolved | default: context.constants.CAPTCHA_DEFAULT_PROVIDER | strip | downcase
  assign resolved = resolved | default: ''
  return resolved
%}
